	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11523"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 104<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=991.msg11523#msg11523"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=991.msg11523#msg11523">Re: Rodcet Nife Allstars</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #138 on:</b> October 01, 2004, 06:38:11 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=991.msg11440#msg11440">Quote from: Hemdall on September 27, 2004, 10:33:10 am</a></div><div class="quote">Wrong Del.  My vote is for Dyvim.</div>Yes but I know better, since I played more, was more observant and was an integral part of killing new mobs on RN for like 80% of the new encounters found.<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">I would like to mention Dwilgar as a shaman allstar.  Reading through this thread, I do not even recognize the shaman mentioned in the various posts.  I would say in the early formative years of the shaman, Dwilgar would have to be placed at or near the top of the list.  Not only for his in-game actions but also for his out-of-game support for shaman causes</div>Well Dwilgar was quasi-mentorish to Reia back then, and they were definitely the top of the class back then. However Reia was around a lot longer, and definitely surpassed Dwilgar later on. Would Dwilgar have been able to do the same things had he played? Very possible, but I doubt he could have surpassed.<br /><br />Most classes are pretty easy to teach to observant people, in which case there&#039;s very little difference between &quot;apprentice and master&quot; if you will, except the attention paid at the time. Originally I was by far the best raid cleric in Ascent, but people like Chauey and Winnikin picked everything up pretty fast, and later on Lumilla (who knew a lot even before joining) joined the club. Many others got pretty good too, but we knew essentially all the same stuff, and I tended to focus more on other things than actual healing, which dropped me as the worst cleric of the &quot;we pay attention and want to learn&quot; bunch.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Also, OLD SCHOOL &gt; current any day.</div>Dunno why it would be. I think RN peaked in the pecking order of servers during the Dyvim/Crimshines and then again with Ascent (top 5 server at both times). There is no reason it couldn&#039;t do that again (though I don&#039;t see DA/EiE being the type that would be able - or interested in - pulling it off).<br /><br />Ascent is almost certainly the most powerful guild on WoW beta alliance, with AL coming as a close #2. I don&#039;t really see what this should get us in live. A cookie for being oldschool? Beta school even omg! Oldschool means absolutely jack shit when you talk skill, unless it&#039;s just old content and the old school really has to figure out all the key class strats.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
